// =============================================================================
// Search Job: Full-Year Outbound Connection Analysis (Historical C2 Hunt)
// Threats:  Nation-State Cyber Espionage (DNS Tunneling, C2 over HTTPS)
// MITRE:    TA0011 Command and Control, T1071 Application Layer Protocol
// Companion to Article 03: Hunting at Machine Speed
// https://socautomators.substack.com/p/hunting-at-machine-speed-kql-on-the
// =============================================================================
//
// Some hunts need time windows that exceed what interactive KQL can handle.
// A query spanning a full year of firewall session logs will time out in the
// portal. Submit this as a Sentinel Search Job — it runs asynchronously
// against the data lake and delivers results to a dedicated search results
// table. Plan for hours of latency, not minutes.
//
// Hypothesis: Long-lived, low-volume outbound connections to a small number of
// destinations are characteristic of low-and-slow C2 channels that survive
// for months. Filter on duration > 90 days, very few distinct source devices,
// and sustained connection counts.
//
// HOW TO RUN:
// Submit this as a Search Job via the Sentinel portal or REST API. Do not
// execute interactively against a full year of CommonSecurityLog data — the
// volume will exceed interactive query limits.
//
// Parameters:
//   lookback      - historical window (designed for 365d Search Job)
//   min_duration  - minimum sustained-connection duration in days
//   max_sources   - upper bound on distinct source devices (C2 is narrow)
//   min_count     - minimum connection volume threshold
// =============================================================================

CommonSecurityLog
| where TimeGenerated > ago(365d)
| where DeviceAction == "Allow"
| where DestinationPort in (443, 80, 53, 8080)
| summarize
    ConnectionCount = count(),
    BytesSent = sum(SentBytes),
    BytesReceived = sum(ReceivedBytes),
    FirstConnection = min(TimeGenerated),
    LastConnection = max(TimeGenerated),
    DistinctSourceDevices = dcount(DeviceName)
    by DestinationIP, DestinationPort
| extend DurationDays = datetime_diff('day', LastConnection, FirstConnection)
| where DurationDays > 90
| where DistinctSourceDevices <= 3
| where ConnectionCount > 500
| sort by DurationDays desc, ConnectionCount desc
